<section class="box-exercise">
<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Organic_Chemistry/Organic_Chemistry_(Morsch_et_al.)/20:_Carboxylic_Acids_and_Nitriles/20.02:_Structure_and_Properties_of_Carboxylic_Acids" class="mt-section"><span id="Exercise_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B2.7D.5C)"></span><h5 class="box-legend editable"><span class="lt-icon-default">Exercise \(\PageIndex{2}\)</span></h5>

<p>What percentage <span style="transform:scaleX(1.14638);">of propanoic acid (CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>COOH) is dissociated into its conjugate base in a 0.20 M aqueous solution?</span> <span class="q-box">K<sub>a</sub> = 1.32 x 10&#8315;&#8309;</span></p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong class="emphasis bold">Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p class="lt-chem-36551">From the acid equilibrium expression we get that:</p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">[CH&#8323;CH&#8322;COO&#8315;][H<sub>3</sub>O&#8314;]/[CH&#8323;CH&#8322;COOH] = K<sub>a</sub> = 1.32 x 10&#8315;&#8309;</span></p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">[X][X]/[0.20 M - X] = 1.32 x 10&#8315;&#8309;</span></p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">Assume X is small compared to 0.20 M</span></p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">[X]<sup>2</sup>/[0.20 M] = 1.32 x 10&#8315;&#8309;</span></p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">X = [CH&#8323;CH&#8322;COO&#8315;] = 1.62 x 10&#8315;<sup>3</sup> M</span></p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">[CH&#8323;CH&#8322;COO&#8315;] </span>/<span class="q-box"> [CH&#8323;CH&#8322;COOH]</span> X 100 = %Disassociation <span> </span></p>

    <p class="lt-chem-36551"><span class="q-box">1.62 x 10&#8315;<sup>3</sup> M / 0.20 M X 100 = <strong>0.812%</strong></span></p>
    </dd>
</dl>
